    45   * Rate limiting filter, with configurable threshold above which 
non-privileged clients will be
    46   * dropped. This feature enables cutting off non-standard and 
potentially harmful clients in case of
    47   * system overload. Since it is critical to always allow client 
registrations and heartbeats into
    48   * the system, which at the same time are relatively cheap operations, 
the rate limiting is applied
    49   * only to full and delta registry fetches. Furthermore, since delta 
fetches are much smaller than
    50   * full fetches, and if not served my result in following full registry 
fetch from the client, they
    51   * have relatively higher priority. This is implemented by two parallel 
rate limiters, one for
    52   * overall number of full/delta fetches (higher threshold) and one for 
full fetches only (low
    53   * threshold).
    54   *
    55   * <p>The client is identified by {@link 
AbstractEurekaIdentity#AUTH_NAME_HEADER_KEY} HTTP header
    56   * value. The privileged group by default contains:
    57   *
    58   * <ul>
